---
import LegalLayout from '../components/LegalLayout.astro';
import { SITE, LEGAL } from '../data/site';

const op = LEGAL.operator;
const email = LEGAL.contactEmail;
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  eyebrow="Legal"
  path="/privacy/"
  lede="How DummyLead collects, uses, stores, and shares information, and the choices and rights you have over your data."
  description="DummyLead's Privacy Policy: what we collect, how we use call recordings, transcripts and seed data, who we share it with, and your data rights."
>
  <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    DummyLead ("DummyLead", "we", "us", or "our") is a seed-lead monitoring
    service operated by {op}, {LEGAL.operatorDescriptor}. References to
    <strong>{SITE.domain}</strong>, the dashboard at
    <strong>{SITE.appUrl.replace('https://', '')}</strong>, and the DummyLead
    service are all covered by this policy.
  </p>
  <p>
    For privacy questions, requests, or complaints, contact us at
    <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>. The entity responsible for your data
    (the "controller") is {op}.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Scope, and a note on how this service works</h2>
  <p>
    DummyLead lets a customer place decoy "seed" leads, with their own inbox and
    phone line, into a lead flow, then records the calls, texts, and emails that
    reach those seeds so the customer can audit how leads are handled. This means
    DummyLead processes two very different kinds of information:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Account data</strong> about our customers (the businesses and
      people who buy and operate DummyLead), and
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Captured-interaction data</strong> about the third parties who
      contact a seed, which can include sales reps, partners, buyers, and other
      callers who are not DummyLead customers.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    For captured-interaction data, the customer who placed the seed decides why
    and how that data is collected, so the customer is the controller and
    DummyLead acts as a <strong>processor</strong> (<em>encargado</em>) on the
    customer's behalf, under the Data Processing terms in our
    <a href="/terms/">Terms of Service</a>. The customer is responsible for
    having a lawful basis to record and for complying with all consent and
    recording laws. See our <a href="/acceptable-use/">Acceptable Use Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Information we collect</h2>
  <h3>Information you give us</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Account and contact details</strong>: name, work email, company,
      phone number, and the contents of messages you send us.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Seed configuration</strong>: the personas, identities, inboxes,
      and phone numbers you ask us to create and place on your behalf.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Billing details</strong>: your plan, seed counts, and billing
      contact. Card and bank details are collected and stored by our payment
      processor, not by us (see Section 6).
    </li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Information we collect automatically</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Usage and device data</strong>: log data, IP address, browser and
      device type, pages viewed, and timestamps, used to run and secure the
      service.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Cookies and similar technologies</strong>: see Section 8.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Captured-interaction data (third parties)</h3>
  <p>
    When someone contacts a seed lead, DummyLead may record and store, on the
    customer's behalf:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Inbound and outbound phone numbers and caller-ID information;</li>
    <li>Call audio recordings and their transcripts;</li>
    <li>SMS/text message content and metadata;</li>
    <li>Email content, headers, and metadata;</li>
    <li>
      Timing, frequency, and channel of each contact, and derived signals such
      as response time, attempt counts, spam-risk scores, and SHAKEN/STIR
      attestation grades.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. How we use information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To create, place, and operate seed leads you configure;</li>
    <li>
      To capture, transcribe, score, and present the interactions that reach
      your seeds in your dashboard, timelines, recordings, and reports;
    </li>
    <li>To provide, maintain, secure, and improve the service;</li>
    <li>To bill you, prevent fraud, and enforce our Terms;</li>
    <li>To respond to your requests and provide support;</li>
    <li>
      To comply with legal obligations and to establish, exercise, or defend
      legal claims.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do <strong>not</strong> sell personal data, and we do not use call
    recordings, transcripts, or captured-interaction data to train third-party
    advertising models.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Legal bases</h2>
  <p>
    Where data-protection law requires a legal basis, we rely on: performance of
    our contract with you; your consent (which you may withdraw); our legitimate
    interests in operating and securing the service; and compliance with legal
    obligations. For captured-interaction data, the customer is responsible for
    establishing the lawful basis and any required consent of the people
    recorded.
  </p>

  <h2>6. How we share information</h2>
  <p>We share information only as needed to run DummyLead:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Service providers (sub-processors)</strong> that host our
      infrastructure, deliver telephony and SMS, transcribe audio, score spam
      and attestation, send email, and process payments. These providers are
      bound by contract to protect the data and use it only to provide their
      service to us.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Payment processor</strong>: card and bank data is handled directly
      by our payment processor (for example, Stripe) under their own terms and
      privacy policy. We receive only limited billing metadata.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Legal and safety</strong>: where required by law, to respond to
      lawful requests, or to protect rights, safety, and the integrity of the
      service.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Business transfers</strong>: if the service is acquired or
      reorganized, data may transfer as part of that transaction.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>7. International transfers</h2>
  <p>
    DummyLead is operated from the United States and uses service providers that
    may store or process data in other countries. Where we
    transfer personal data across borders, we use providers that offer
    appropriate safeguards. By using the service you understand your information
    may be processed outside your country of residence.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    The marketing site uses only the cookies and local storage needed to make
    pages work and to understand aggregate traffic. The dashboard uses cookies
    that are strictly necessary to keep you signed in and secure. You can control
    cookies through your browser settings; blocking strictly necessary cookies
    may break sign-in.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Data retention</h2>
  <p>
    We keep account data for as long as your account is active and as needed to
    provide the service, then for a limited period afterward to meet legal, tax,
    and dispute-resolution obligations. Captured-interaction data, including
    recordings and transcripts, is retained according to your plan and settings
    and is deleted on your instruction or within a reasonable period after your
    account closes, unless we are required to keep it longer by law.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Security</h2>
  <p>
    We use technical and organizational measures designed to protect information,
    including encryption in transit, access controls, and least-privilege
    practices. No method of transmission or storage is perfectly secure, so we
    cannot guarantee absolute security.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct, delete,
    port, or restrict the processing of your personal data, to object to certain
    processing, and to withdraw consent. If you are in the EEA/UK or California,
    you may have these rights under the GDPR or CCPA/CPRA.
  </p>
  <p>
    To exercise any right, email <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>. We will
    respond within the timeframe required by applicable law. If a request
    concerns captured-interaction data held on a customer's behalf, we will refer
    the request to that customer (the controller) and assist them in responding.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Children</h2>
  <p>
    DummyLead is a business tool and is not directed to children. We do not
    knowingly collect personal data from anyone under 18. If you believe a child
    has provided us information, contact us and we will delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>13. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy from time to time. When we make material changes we
    will update the effective date above and, where appropriate, notify you. Your
    continued use of the service after an update means you accept the revised
    policy.
  </p>

  <h2>14. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    {op}<br />
    Email: <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>
  </p>

  <div class="legal-callout">
    <p>
      <strong>Not legal advice.</strong> This document is a starting point
      tailored to DummyLead and is not a substitute for review by a qualified
      attorney familiar with the privacy laws of the countries where your
      customers operate.
    </p>
  </div>
</LegalLayout>
